===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Christianity|Islam|Judaism|sometimes|capitalized}} The [[final#Adjective|final]] [[trial#Noun|trial]] of all [[humankind]], both the [[living#Adjective|living]] and the [[dead#Adjective|dead]], by [[God]] [[expect]]ed to [[take place]] at the [[end of the world]], when each is [[reward#Verb|rewarded]] or [[punish]]ed according to their [[merit#Noun|merits]].
#: {{synonyms|en|apocalypse|Armageddon|day of judgment|doomsday|Final Judgment|final reckoning|Great Assize<lb:archaic>|Last Judgment}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=In the Year 2525|author=w:Zager and Evans|year=1968|passage=If God's a-coming, he ought to make it by then / Maybe he'll look around himself and say / “Guess it's time for the '''judgement day'''!”}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=1999 [title]|album=1999|author=[[w:Prince (musician)|Prince]]|year=1982|passage=But when I woke up this morning / I could have sworn it was '''judgement day'''}}

